Commit 1e91845d6f37d8bce671d62c14f4390324da3659 (release 0.9.5), MIT licence (LICENSE, Copyright (c) 2026 mickys).
Imported: src/ and vt/ and LICENSE. Left out: the upstream tools, trace interposers, test streams, benchmark data and
documentation (about 100 MB), none of which the library needs.

Changes made here, in this order of importance:
  vt/nvencvt.c   NVEncVT_RegisterDecoders(): registers only the decoders, for the decode service (appended before
                 load_conf).
                 EnableLowLatencyRateControl: declared as a selection property of the H.264 and HEVC encoders, accepted by
                 SetProperty / CopyProperty and listed among the supported properties. A session that sets it is real-time
                 with no B pictures. Without the declaration VideoToolbox drops the encoder from the candidates of any
                 client that asks for low-latency rate control (FFmpeg's low_delay, Sunshine), and answers -12902.

  src/hevcparse.c  scaling_list_data(): scaling_list_pred_matrix_id_delta is checked against its range (0..matrixId, matrixId / 3
                 for 32x32) before it is used as an index; a hostile SPS or PPS used to read outside the list array.
                 tools/test_nvenc_parsers.py. To be sent upstream.

